// webOS drew the ends of a selection as small shields that point at the text -
// topmarker.png and bottommarker.png, 18x15, a band of full width tapering to
// a point. This is that shape on Chromium's 32 unit canvas: legacy's 14x11 of
// ink scaled to the width, so the proportions are its own.
//
// Pointing up in all three, because these handles are drawn below the line
// they belong to. Legacy put the one at the start of a selection above the
// line and pointed it down, which is a matter of where the handle is placed
// rather than how it is drawn - see TouchHandle's layout.

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 32,
MOVE_TO, 16, 0,
LINE_TO, 32, 13.7,
V_LINE_TO, 25.1,
H_LINE_TO, 0,
V_LINE_TO, 13.7,
CLOSE
